<article class="env-lemma" id="0A3Q">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A3Q">Lemma <span data-tag="0A3Q">59.83.8</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0A52" data-tag="0A52">59.83.1</a> assume $X$ reduced. Let $j : U \to X$ an open immersion. Let $\ell $ be a prime number and $\mathcal{F} = j_!\underline{\mathbf{Z}/\ell \mathbf{Z}}$. Then statements (<a href="/tag/0A53" data-tag="0A53">1</a>) – (<a href="/tag/0A5A" data-tag="0A5A">8</a>) hold for $\mathcal{F}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The difference with Lemma <a href="/tag/03SG" data-tag="03SG">59.83.7</a> is that here we do not assume $X$ is smooth. Let $\nu : X^\nu \to X$ be the normalization morphism. Then $\nu $ is finite (Varieties, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BXR" data-tag="0BXR">33.27.1</a>) and $X^\nu $ is smooth (Varieties, Lemma <a href="/tag/0B8Y" data-tag="0B8Y">33.43.8</a>). Let $j^\nu : U^\nu \to X^\nu $ be the inverse image of $U$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/03SG" data-tag="03SG">59.83.7</a> the result holds for $j^\nu _!\underline{\mathbf{Z}/\ell \mathbf{Z}}$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0A5D" data-tag="0A5D">59.83.5</a> the result holds for $\nu _*j^\nu _!\underline{\mathbf{Z}/\ell \mathbf{Z}}$. In general it won't be true that $\nu _*j^\nu _!\underline{\mathbf{Z}/\ell \mathbf{Z}}$ is equal to $j_!\underline{\mathbf{Z}/\ell \mathbf{Z}}$ but we can work around this as follows. As $X$ is reduced the morphism $\nu : X^\nu \to X$ is an isomorphism over a dense open $j' : X' \to X$ (Varieties, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BXR" data-tag="0BXR">33.27.1</a>). Over this open we have agreement 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  (j')^{-1}(\nu _*j^\nu _!\underline{\mathbf{Z}/\ell \mathbf{Z}}) = (j')^{-1}(j_!\underline{\mathbf{Z}/\ell \mathbf{Z}})  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Using Lemma <a href="/tag/0GJA" data-tag="0GJA">59.83.6</a> twice for $j' : X' \to X$ and the sheaves above we conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>